  "question": {
    "text": "Let a circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;in complex plane pass through the points <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>i</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>i</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mfenced><mrow><mo>&#8800;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is a point on <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;such that the line through&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to the line through <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>, then <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>arg</mi><mfenced><mi>z</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is equal to",
