  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>z</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>C</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>&#8801;</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/dbf9435b-4388-4da7-b025-5daadc542be2-image.png\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 141px;\" /></p><p>Slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Slope of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p>Now, equation of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>AP</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>is</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>Since&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi></math> lies on circle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>2</mn><mfenced><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>7</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>arg</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>tan</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mfenced><mfrac><mn>24</mn><mn>7</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>-</mo><mi>&#960;</mi></math></p>",
